1
00:04:26,666 --> 00:04:32,666
Zaniness has no limits.

2
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:59,333
Animaniacs: Wakko's Wish is a animation, music,
comedy film directed by Liz Holzman.

3
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
The Warner Brothers (and the Warner Sister) go on a quest to find a
fallen wishing star to help Dot with her illness.

4
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:52,666
Unfortunately the rest of the town, including an evil king, also hear about the
star and want to get to it first to have their own wishes come true.

5
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
It's a race against time and it's up to the three
zany siblings to get there first.

6
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Yakko Warner / Pinky / Dr. Otto Scratchansniff (voice), played by Rob Paulsen.

7
00:31:06,666 --> 00:31:12,666
Wakko Warner (voice), played by Jess Harnell.

8
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:39,333
Dot Warner / Marita Hippo / Hello Nurse / Mindy's
Mother (voice), played by Tress MacNeille.

9
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Brain / Squit (voice), played by Maurice LaMarche.

10
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Mindy (voice), played by Nancy Cartwright.

11
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Various (voice), played by Frank Welker.

12
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Wakko's Wish (also known as Animaniacs: Wakko's Wish and originally titled as Wakko's Wakko Wish) is a 1999 American animated musical comedy-adventure fantasy
direct-to-video film based on the 1993–1998 animated series Animaniacs, and was the last work related to the series before the 2020 revival of the series.

13
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
It relocates all of the Animaniacs characters to a quasi-19th century fairy tale world and
portrays their race to find the wishing star that will grant them a wish.

14
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
The film was first released on VHS on December 21, 1999.

15
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
It contains 10 original songs and features a majority of the voice
cast reprising their respective roles from the TV show.

16
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
The film explores themes of woman director, sick relative, wishing on a star.

17
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
